WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:02.590
Speaker 1: This is fascinating.

00:00:02.590 --> 00:00:08.040
Last week, when Ron DeSantis responded to
Trump's attack on him by saying, I don't spend

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:12.650
my time attacking other Republicans, DeSantis
took the high road as we discussed.

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:18.779
I told you, this isn't going to work for DeSantis,
and I have expressed concerns previously that

00:00:18.779 --> 00:00:24.880
in a national campaign, DeSantis, who lacks
all charisma, I mean, just completely uncharismatic.

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:25.880
I don't know how to.

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:31.310
Santos faces off against Trump and the nicknames
and the attacks in a national campaign.

00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:33.180
I'm not the only one saying this.

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:35.010
This is really interesting.

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:41.110
There's a New York Times article published
two days ago called DeSantis Challenge When

00:00:41.110 --> 00:00:44.030
and How to Counterattack Trump.

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:47.280
The article is by Michael Bender and Maggie
Haberman.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:52.010
And in this article, they actually address
this issue.

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:56.030
He's trying to take the high road, but that
is not likely to work.

00:00:56.030 --> 00:01:01.870
And there's a paragraph that says some deep
pocketed Republican donors have privately

00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:09.150
expressed concern about how DeSantis will
perform when forced to directly engage with

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:17.770
an opponent as combative and unbothered by
traditional rules of decorum as Mr. Trump.

00:01:17.770 --> 00:01:23.600
Liam Donovan, a Republican strategist, said
No Republican has ever emerged from an exchange

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:26.729
with Donald Trump looking stronger.

00:01:26.729 --> 00:01:31.610
So the natural tendency is to deflect attacks
and avoid confrontation.

00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:36.670
That's easy to do, maybe wise, when Trump's
barbs are confined to truth social.

00:01:36.670 --> 00:01:41.960
The question is what happens when DeSantis
finds himself on a debate stage opposite Trump

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:43.229
and Republicans vote?

00:01:43.229 --> 00:01:46.869
Republican voters want to see whether they
are getting what they were promised.

00:01:46.869 --> 00:01:51.189
I think this article is exactly right, and
I think that the Republicans who are bringing

00:01:51.189 --> 00:01:57.380
this up are 100% justified in being concerned
with this.

00:01:57.380 --> 00:02:03.119
And the article mentions all of these, you
know, different attacks that Trump launched

00:02:03.119 --> 00:02:08.280
against challengers in 2016, insinuating that
Ted Cruz, his father, was linked to the assassination

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:14.480
of John F Kennedy, calling Ben Carson pathological,
making fun of the appearance of Ted Cruz,

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:18.150
his wife, and of Rand Paul and so on and so
forth.

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:19.620
This is exactly right.

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:25.650
And so while I believe that, at least in theory
right now, Ron DeSantis is well positioned

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:30.110
for a run against Trump, if he announces and
if he takes the campaign seriously and he'll

00:02:30.110 --> 00:02:32.160
he has a shot, there's no doubt.

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:36.590
But if they emerge as the frontrunners, Trump
and DeSantis, and if they end up on stage

00:02:36.590 --> 00:02:41.010
against each other and DeSantis does this
high road stuff while Trump brutally attacks

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:44.319
the Santos and he will, it doesn't look good
for DeSantis.

00:02:44.319 --> 00:02:48.730
I don't actually believe that Republican voters
are going to be swayed by a guy who takes

00:02:48.730 --> 00:02:49.730
the high road.

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:54.670
I think they want to see who here brings the
sort of like, you know, what they what they

00:02:54.670 --> 00:02:58.070
wrongly believe to be alpha energy and whatever
else.

00:02:58.070 --> 00:03:01.200
And I don't think the Santos taking the high
road will work.

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:06.200
And DeSantis does need to figure out how do
I attack Trump, When do I attack Trump or

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:07.560
the chance that he has it?

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:09.819
This thing is going to very quickly evaporate.

00:03:09.819 --> 00:03:10.880
Let me know your thoughts.

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:14.209
What should DeSantis approach be?

00:03:14.209 --> 00:03:17.500
And we will certainly have time to discuss
this further.

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:23.300
Trump has started to go after DeSantis in
casual conversations, they say, describing

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:28.260
him as all sorts of different strange things
based on his physical appearance.

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:29.849
So Trump seems to be winding it up.

00:03:29.849 --> 00:03:33.580
And even though Trump says he's not thinking
about it, all of the indications are that

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:34.920
he is Trump's going to be ready.

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:38.099
This is you know, Trump's not going to be
ready with that health care plan that we were

00:03:38.099 --> 00:03:39.650
going to get in August of 2020.

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:42.930
I'm not holding my breath waiting for that
health care plan.

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:46.783
Trump is going to be ready for how to attack
Ron DeSantis, and DeSantis has to figure out

00:03:46.783 --> 00:03:46.792
what to do.

